# Test design

Name tests as business outcomes: `should prevent candidate creation when mandatory email is missing`. Never `test1`.

Structure: Arrange, Act, Assert. Each test needs a clear objective, preconditions, meaningful assertions, and cleanup only when the test created shared state.

Tag with `@smoke` and `@regression` via Playwright `tag` / title annotations where appropriate.

Cover positive, negative, boundary, validation, authorization/RBAC, errors, state transitions, data integrity, UI, and API/UI integration when relevant.

Tests call flows or page actions — never locators.

```typescript
test('should prevent candidate creation when mandatory email is missing', async ({ candidateFlow }) => {
  const result = await candidateFlow.createCandidate({ ...validCandidate, email: '' });
  await expect(result.validationError).toBeVisible();
});
```
